# =============================================================================
# StoryBook Studio — client environment
# =============================================================================
# Copy to `client/.env`. Vite reads this file from the client workspace.
#
# EVERY value here is PUBLIC: Vite inlines each VITE_* variable into the browser
# bundle, where anyone can read it. Never put a Gemini, Kie.ai, storage,
# database or JWT secret in this file — those belong in server/.env, and a
# contract test fails the build if one reaches the bundle.
#
# In development the client talks to the API through Vite's proxy, so
# VITE_API_BASE_URL can be left unset and requests stay same-origin — which is
# what lets the refresh cookie work without CORS.
# =============================================================================

# Leave this unset for local development.
#
# Unset, the client calls a relative /api/v1 path, which Vite's dev proxy
# forwards to the server — so every request is SAME-ORIGIN. That matters: the
# refresh cookie is httpOnly and SameSite-scoped, and a browser will not send it
# across origins. Point this at http://localhost:5000 while the page is served
# from 127.0.0.1:5173 and the two count as different sites, so the cookie is
# never sent, /auth/refresh answers 401 forever, and the session never sticks.
#
# Set it only when the client is deployed on a different origin from the API,
# and make sure CORS_ORIGIN on the server names that origin.
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://api.example.com/api/v1

# VITE_APP_NAME=StoryBook Studio
